{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azure-cognitive-services/form-recognizer/layout-3.1","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:04.014Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azure-cognitive-services/form-recognizer/layout-3.1/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azure-cognitive-services/form-recognizer/layout-3.1/about"},"readme":"## About\n\n[Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services) is a set of APIs, SDKs and container images that enables developers to integrate ready-made AI directly into their applications. Azure AI services contains a broad set of capabilities including text analytics; facial detection, speech and vision recognition; natural language understanding, and more.\n\nContainer support in Azure AI services allow developers to use the same rich APIs that are available in Azure but with the flexibility that comes with containers. See [Container support in Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services-containers) for details.\n\nDocument Intelligence is part of Azure AI services that lets you build automated data processing software using machine learning technology. Identify and extract text, key/value pairs, selection marks, tables, and structure from your documents—the service outputs structured data that includes the relationships in the original file, bounding boxes, confidence and more. You quickly get accurate results that are tailored to your specific content without heavy manual intervention or extensive data science expertise. Use Document Intelligence to automate data entry in your applications and enrich your documents search capabilities. For more information, see [Document Intelligence API Documentation](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cognitive-services/form-recognizer/overview?tabs=v2-1).\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `latest`\ndocker pull mcr.microsoft.com/azure-cognitive-services/form-recognizer/layout\n\n## Related repositories\n\n+ [Azure AI services Images](https://hub.docker.com/_/microsoft-azure-cognitive-services): Azure AI services is a set of APIs, SDKs and container images that enables developers to integrate ready-made AI directly into their applications.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSee the [configuration documentation]() for how to configure this image.\n\n## Usage\n\nSee the [How-to]() for how to use this image.\n\nAlso see the [set of samples](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2043312&clcid=0x409) to help getting started with Azure AI services.\n\n## Related Information\n\n+ [Document Intelligence Azure Cognitive Service](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cognitive-services/form-recognizer/)\n+ [Container Support in Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services-containers)\n+ [Azure AI services](http://aka.ms/cognitive-services)\n+ [Azure Portal](http://portal.azure.com)\n\n## Support\n\nReport feedback or issues on [Stack Overflow](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2056278) using tag azure-cognitive-services.\n\n## License\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)\n\n\nNotice: Copyright © Microsoft Corporation 2020. This Azure AI services Container image is made available to you under the [terms governing your subscription to Microsoft Azure Services](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2018657) (including the [Online Services Terms](https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2018760)). If you do not have a valid Azure subscription, then you may not use this container.","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-11T08:46:24.5592402+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"Other","links":[{"name":"licence","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/licensing/terms/product/ForOnlineServices/EAEAS"}],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"28K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentT